WEBVTT

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:04.186
In under two minutes, you will invite people to help run your contest.

00:00:04.186 --> 00:00:05.253
We start on the map.

00:00:06.155 --> 00:00:09.441
Open your web browser, and go to SoCal Lights dot app.

00:00:11.538 --> 00:00:13.969
This is the SoCal Lights home page.

00:00:13.969 --> 00:00:16.468
A message asks to use your location.

00:00:16.468 --> 00:00:17.819
Tap Use my location.

00:00:19.729 --> 00:00:22.098
Your browser asks for permission.

00:00:22.098 --> 00:00:22.795
Tap Allow.

00:00:26.733 --> 00:00:29.100
Look at the top right corner of the map.

00:00:29.100 --> 00:00:30.254
See the three dots?

00:00:30.254 --> 00:00:30.774
Tap them.

00:00:33.476 --> 00:00:35.368
In the menu, tap Contests.

00:00:37.167 --> 00:00:37.765
Tap Mine.

00:00:37.765 --> 00:00:39.617
These are the contests you run.

00:00:41.301 --> 00:00:43.206
Tap Manage, next to your contest.

00:00:43.206 --> 00:00:44.494
This is your dashboard.

00:00:46.394 --> 00:00:47.014
Tap Team.

00:00:47.014 --> 00:00:49.865
Co-organizers get the same dashboard you have.

00:00:51.674 --> 00:00:54.774
Type their email, and tap Add co-organizer.

00:00:58.421 --> 00:01:02.403
They get an email like this one, with one button to open the dashboard.

00:01:03.404 --> 00:01:06.161
Judges are added on the Judges tab.

00:01:06.161 --> 00:01:07.003
Tap Judges.

00:01:08.797 --> 00:01:11.618
Type a judge's email, and tap Add judge.

00:01:15.286 --> 00:01:19.756
Your judge gets an invitation like this one, with a button that opens their ballot.

00:01:20.756 --> 00:01:22.904
Next up: Announce winners.
